IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `loa-dates`

-- Limitation of Actions Act 1936 (SA) -- the rules a person bringing a claim meets: no limitation period for child abuse
-- (s 3A, with the 2018 transitional rules for claims already barred), the periods for the kinds of action a claim is
-- brought as (ss 33-38), the defendant's absence (s 39), legal disability (s 45), the notice a child must give and what
-- follows (s 45A), absence or imprisonment of the claimant (s 46), an action that survives for an estate (s 46A), a
-- short time limit in another law (s 47), the court's power to extend (s 48) and to dispense with a notice before
-- action (s 50), and the defamation rules (ss 37, 37A, 37B).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in loa-seat.l4 (the person bringing the action), which IMPORTs it
-- and restates no rule. Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS are named outcomes (enumerations), dates or numbers, never MAYBE BOOLEAN, so no NOTHING-kind tag is used.
-- Where the text says no in its own words the outcome begins "no:"; where it does not answer, the outcome says "the Act
-- does not say" (the 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 rulings, in substance). Judgments the Act leaves to the court ("just",
-- "just and reasonable", "reasonable", "good reason", "materially different", "essential", "major significance") are
-- inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (the current version,
-- 1.7.2021, as the register's unauthorised RTF). State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation of Actions Act 1936`

§§ `Commencement dates the Act and its transitional provisions turn on`

-- s 3A: inserted by the Limitation of Actions (Child Abuse) Amendment Act 2018, in operation 1.2.2019.
`the day s 3A commenced` MEANS `the date` 1 2 2019
-- s 38 (mistake of law or fact): substituted by Act 39/1993, in operation 17.6.1993.
`the day s 38 commenced` MEANS `the date` 17 6 1993
-- s 38(2): substituted by the 1994 amending Act s 4(a), in operation 2.6.1994 (ss 3, 5 and 6 of that Act on 9.6.1994;
-- fork F6: "the commencement of the 1994 amending Act" read as 2 June 1994, the day s 38(2) itself began).
`the day the 1994 amending Act commenced` MEANS `the date` 2 6 1994
-- s 37 as substituted by the Defamation Act 2005, in operation 1.1.2006 (Sch 1 cl 8(1)).
`the day the substituted s 37 commenced` MEANS `the date` 1 1 2006
-- s 37(2)-(4), 37A, 37B: Defamation (Miscellaneous) Amendment Act 2020, in operation 1.7.2021 (Sch 1 cl 5).
`the day the 2020 defamation amendments commenced` MEANS `the date` 1 7 2021

§§ `Part 1A, s 3A -- no limitation period for child abuse actions`

-- s 3A(5): "abuse includes any of the following: (a) sexual abuse; (b) serious physical abuse; (c) psychological abuse
-- related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse." An inclusive list: a kind not listed is not answered.
DECLARE `Kind of abuse` IS ONE OF
    `sexual abuse`
    `serious physical abuse`
    `psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse`
    `physical abuse that was not serious`
    `psychological abuse not related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse`
    `another kind of abuse`

GIVEN `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the abuse is a kind s 3A(5) lists` `the kind of abuse` IF
        `the kind of abuse` EQUALS `sexual abuse`
     OR `the kind of abuse` EQUALS `serious physical abuse`
     OR `the kind of abuse` EQUALS `psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse`

DECLARE `Child abuse answer` IS ONE OF
    `no time limit: an action for damages for death or personal injury resulting from abuse suffered as a child may be brought at any time and is not subject to any limitation period (s 3A(1)); the court may still dismiss or stay it if the lapse of time makes a fair trial impossible (s 3A(4))`
    `s 3A does not reach this: it covers abuse suffered while the person abused was a child, under 18 (s 3A(1), s 3(1)); the ordinary periods apply`
    `the Act does not say: abuse "includes" sexual abuse, serious physical abuse and psychological abuse related to them (s 3A(5)), and the list is not closed`

-- s 3A(1): "An action for damages relating to the death of, or personal injury to, a person resulting from the abuse of
-- the person when the person was a child -- (a) may be brought at any time; and (b) is not subject to a limitation
-- period under this Act, or any other Act or law." s 3(1): "child means a person under the age of 18 years". s 3A(2)
-- and (3): however the claim is brought (tort, contract, statute), and for a death (Civil Liability Act 1936 s 23) or
-- for the estate. "When the person was a child" is a scope limit with no "only" (fork F2).
GIVEN `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`, `the age when abused` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Child abuse answer`
`the s 3A answer for` `the kind of abuse` `at age` `the age when abused` MEANS
    IF `the age when abused` AT LEAST 18
    THEN `s 3A does not reach this: it covers abuse suffered while the person abused was a child, under 18 (s 3A(1), s 3(1)); the ordinary periods apply`
    ELSE IF `the abuse is a kind s 3A(5) lists` `the kind of abuse`
         THEN `no time limit: an action for damages for death or personal injury resulting from abuse suffered as a child may be brought at any time and is not subject to any limitation period (s 3A(1)); the court may still dismiss or stay it if the lapse of time makes a fair trial impossible (s 3A(4))`
         ELSE `the Act does not say: abuse "includes" sexual abuse, serious physical abuse and psychological abuse related to them (s 3A(5)), and the list is not closed`

-- Limitation of Actions (Child Abuse) Amendment Act 2018, Sch 1 cl 2: s 3A applies to a cause of action that accrued
-- before or after 1 February 2019, "including where a limitation period previously applying ... had expired". cl 3(1):
-- an action on a previously barred cause of action may be commenced even though (a) another action had been started
-- but not finalised, (b) another was started but discontinued, (c) a judgment was given on the limitation ground, or
-- (d) an action was dismissed on that ground. cl 3(2): in cases (c) and (d) only if a court, "being satisfied that it
-- is just and reasonable to do so, grants permission".
DECLARE `Earlier proceedings on the claim` IS ONE OF
    `there was no earlier action or judgment`
    `an action was started but not finalised before 1 February 2019`
    `an action was started but discontinued before 1 February 2019`
    `a judgment was given on the ground that the limitation period had expired`
    `an action was dismissed on the ground that the limitation period had expired`

DECLARE `Previously barred answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: section 3A applies whenever the cause of action accrued, even if a limitation period had expired before 1 February 2019 (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 2)`
    `yes: you may commence an action even though an earlier action on the claim was started, whether or not it was finalised or was discontinued (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 3(1)(a), (b))`
    `yes: the court has granted permission to commence the action despite the earlier judgment or dismissal on the limitation ground (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 3(2))`
    `not without permission: after a judgment or dismissal on the limitation ground, a new action may be commenced only if a court, satisfied that it is just and reasonable, grants permission (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 3(2))`
    `this transitional rule does not help: section 3A does not apply to the claim on these facts`

GIVEN `the s 3A answer` IS A `Child abuse answer`
      `the earlier proceedings` IS AN `Earlier proceedings on the claim`
      `the court grants permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Previously barred answer`
`the 2018 transitional answer` `the s 3A answer` `the earlier proceedings` `the court grants permission` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the s 3A answer` EQUALS `no time limit: an action for damages for death or personal injury resulting from abuse suffered as a child may be brought at any time and is not subject to any limitation period (s 3A(1)); the court may still dismiss or stay it if the lapse of time makes a fair trial impossible (s 3A(4))`)
    THEN `this transitional rule does not help: section 3A does not apply to the claim on these facts`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the earlier proceedings`
         WHEN `there was no earlier action or judgment` THEN `yes: section 3A applies whenever the cause of action accrued, even if a limitation period had expired before 1 February 2019 (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 2)`
         WHEN `an action was started but not finalised before 1 February 2019` THEN `yes: you may commence an action even though an earlier action on the claim was started, whether or not it was finalised or was discontinued (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 3(1)(a), (b))`
         WHEN `an action was started but discontinued before 1 February 2019` THEN `yes: you may commence an action even though an earlier action on the claim was started, whether or not it was finalised or was discontinued (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 3(1)(a), (b))`
         OTHERWISE
             IF `the court grants permission`
             THEN `yes: the court has granted permission to commence the action despite the earlier judgment or dismissal on the limitation ground (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 3(2))`
             ELSE `not without permission: after a judgment or dismissal on the limitation ground, a new action may be commenced only if a court, satisfied that it is just and reasonable, grants permission (2018 Act Sch 1 cl 3(2))`

§§ `Parts 4 to 6 -- the period for each kind of action`

-- One action is one of these kinds. s 36(1): an action in which "the damages claimed consist of or include damages in
-- respect of personal injuries" is a personal injury action, whether it is in contract or tort; s 36(2): "personal
-- injuries include any disease and any impairment of a person's physical or mental condition". s 35 lists simple
-- contract, award, account, tort, arrears of rent not by deed, arrears of interest, damages for such arrears, seamen's
-- wages, money levied on a fieri facias or for an escape. Parts 2 and 3 (land, rent, mortgages, trusts) are out.
DECLARE `Kind of action` IS ONE OF
    `damages for death or personal injury resulting from abuse suffered as a child`
    `damages that include damages for personal injuries`
    `simple contract, tort, account, or another action listed in s 35, with no damages for personal injuries`
    `defamation`
    `recovery of money paid by mistake or on other restitutionary grounds`
    `recovery of money paid as a tax that was invalid`
    `rent under a lease by deed, or covenant or debt on a bond, other specialty, judgment or recognisance`
    `money secured by a mortgage, judgment or lien or otherwise charged on land, or a legacy`
    `another kind of action`

DECLARE `Period answer` IS ONE OF
    `none: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 3A(1))`
    `3 years after the cause of action accrued (s 36(1))`
    `3 years after the injury first came to your knowledge, because it remained latent (s 36(1a))`
    `6 years after the cause of action accrued (s 35)`
    `1 year running from the date of publication (s 37(1)), extended if a concerns notice is given in its last 56 days (s 37(2), (3))`
    `1 year running from the date of publication (s 37(1))`
    `6 years after the cause of action arose (s 38(1)(a))`
    `6 months after the date of the payment, and it cannot be extended (s 38(2)(a), (3))`
    `15 years after the cause of action accrued or the judgment was recovered, or after the last written acknowledgment or part payment (s 34)`
    `15 years after a present right to receive the money accrued, or after the last payment or written acknowledgment (s 33(1), (2))`
    `not covered: a kind of action this encoding does not cover (Parts 2 and 3: land, rent, mortgages and trusts)`
    `not covered: a restitution claim that arose before 17 June 1993 (s 38(1)(b): the old period or 6 years after 17 June 1993, whichever expired first)`
    `not covered: a tax paid more than four months before 2 June 1994 (s 38(2)(b))`
    `not covered: a publication before 1 January 2006, to which the limitation law before the Defamation Act 2005 applies`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of action`, `the day it accrued` IS A DATE, `latent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Period answer`
`the period for` `the kind` `accrued on` `the day it accrued` `with latency` `latent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `damages for death or personal injury resulting from abuse suffered as a child` THEN `none: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 3A(1))`
    WHEN `damages that include damages for personal injuries` THEN
        IF `latent`
        THEN `3 years after the injury first came to your knowledge, because it remained latent (s 36(1a))`
        ELSE `3 years after the cause of action accrued (s 36(1))`
    WHEN `simple contract, tort, account, or another action listed in s 35, with no damages for personal injuries` THEN `6 years after the cause of action accrued (s 35)`
    WHEN `defamation` THEN
        IF `the day it accrued` `is before` `the day the substituted s 37 commenced`
        THEN `not covered: a publication before 1 January 2006, to which the limitation law before the Defamation Act 2005 applies`
        ELSE IF `the day it accrued` `is before` `the day the 2020 defamation amendments commenced`
             THEN `1 year running from the date of publication (s 37(1))`
             ELSE `1 year running from the date of publication (s 37(1)), extended if a concerns notice is given in its last 56 days (s 37(2), (3))`
    WHEN `recovery of money paid by mistake or on other restitutionary grounds` THEN
        IF `the day it accrued` `is before` `the day s 38 commenced`
        THEN `not covered: a restitution claim that arose before 17 June 1993 (s 38(1)(b): the old period or 6 years after 17 June 1993, whichever expired first)`
        ELSE `6 years after the cause of action arose (s 38(1)(a))`
    WHEN `recovery of money paid as a tax that was invalid` THEN
        IF `the day it accrued` `is before` (`the day the 1994 amending Act commenced` `plus months` (0 MINUS 4))
        THEN `not covered: a tax paid more than four months before 2 June 1994 (s 38(2)(b))`
        ELSE `6 months after the date of the payment, and it cannot be extended (s 38(2)(a), (3))`
    WHEN `rent under a lease by deed, or covenant or debt on a bond, other specialty, judgment or recognisance` THEN `15 years after the cause of action accrued or the judgment was recovered, or after the last written acknowledgment or part payment (s 34)`
    WHEN `money secured by a mortgage, judgment or lien or otherwise charged on land, or a legacy` THEN `15 years after a present right to receive the money accrued, or after the last payment or written acknowledgment (s 33(1), (2))`
    OTHERWISE `not covered: a kind of action this encoding does not cover (Parts 2 and 3: land, rent, mortgages and trusts)`

-- The length of each period in months (ss 33-38).
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of action`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months in the period for` `the kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `damages that include damages for personal injuries` THEN 36
    WHEN `simple contract, tort, account, or another action listed in s 35, with no damages for personal injuries` THEN 72
    WHEN `defamation` THEN 12
    WHEN `recovery of money paid by mistake or on other restitutionary grounds` THEN 72
    WHEN `recovery of money paid as a tax that was invalid` THEN 6
    WHEN `rent under a lease by deed, or covenant or debt on a bond, other specialty, judgment or recognisance` THEN 180
    WHEN `money secured by a mortgage, judgment or lien or otherwise charged on land, or a legacy` THEN 180
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `The facts of one action, and its last day`

-- One action by one person against one person liable. Dates the person does not need are ignored.
DECLARE `Limitation facts` HAS
    `the kind of action` IS A `Kind of action`
    `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE
    `the injury remained latent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the injury first came to the person's knowledge` IS A DATE
    `there was a later acknowledgment or payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment` IS A DATE
    `the person liable was absent from the State when it accrued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person liable has returned to the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the person liable returned` IS A DATE
    `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE
    `the person was mentally incapable after it accrued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the incapacity began` IS A DATE
    `the incapacity has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the incapacity ended` IS A DATE
    `the action survives for a deceased person's estate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the death` IS A DATE
    `the day of the grant of probate or administration` IS A DATE
    `a concerns notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the concerns notice was given` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Last day answer` IS ONE OF
    `the last day to commence the action is` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the time is extended while the incapacity continues, but not beyond 30 years after the right arose (s 45(1), (3)); at the latest` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `there is no last day: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 3A(1))`
    `the time has not started: it runs from the return to the State of the person liable (s 39)`
    `not covered by this encoding`

-- s 39: "If any person against whom there is any such cause of action as is referred to in section 35 or 36 was at
-- the time when the cause of action accrued absent from the State the party entitled to the action may commence it
-- within the time limited by this Act after the return of that person from beyond the seas as if that had been the time
-- at which the cause of action accrued."
GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39 applies to` f IF
        (   f's `the kind of action` EQUALS `damages that include damages for personal injuries`
         OR f's `the kind of action` EQUALS `simple contract, tort, account, or another action listed in s 35, with no damages for personal injuries`)
    AND f's `the person liable was absent from the State when it accrued`

-- The day the cause of action accrued, or the day s 39 treats as that day.
GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the accrual day s 39 gives` f MEANS
    IF `s 39 applies to` f
    THEN f's `the day the person liable returned`
    ELSE f's `the day the cause of action accrued`

-- The day the period runs from: s 36(1a) for a latent injury ("begins to run when the injury first comes to the
-- person's knowledge"), ss 33(2), 34 proviso for a later payment or written acknowledgment. Fork F3: where s 39 also
-- applies, the later of the two days.
GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the period runs from` f MEANS
    IF     f's `the kind of action` EQUALS `damages that include damages for personal injuries`
       AND f's `the injury remained latent`
    THEN `the later of` (`the accrual day s 39 gives` f) `and` (f's `the day the injury first came to the person's knowledge`)
    ELSE IF     (   f's `the kind of action` EQUALS `rent under a lease by deed, or covenant or debt on a bond, other specialty, judgment or recognisance`
                 OR f's `the kind of action` EQUALS `money secured by a mortgage, judgment or lien or otherwise charged on land, or a legacy`)
            AND f's `there was a later acknowledgment or payment`
         THEN `the later of` (`the accrual day s 39 gives` f) `and` (f's `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment`)
         ELSE `the accrual day s 39 gives` f

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the ordinary last day for` f MEANS
    (`the day the period runs from` f) `plus months` (`the months in the period for` (f's `the kind of action`))

-- s 37(2): the 1 year period "is taken to have been extended ... if a concerns notice is given to the proposed defendant
-- on a day (the notice day) within the period of 56 days before the limitation period expires"; s 37(3): "extended for
-- an additional period of 56 days minus any days remaining after the notice day until the 1 year limitation period
-- expires". The Example (notice "7 days before", "6 days left", extended by 50) fixes the count: with the period's last
-- day L and the notice day N, the days remaining are L minus N, so the new last day is N plus 56 days; the window is
-- N from L minus 55 to L (fork F4). Publications on or after 1 July 2021 only (2020 Act Sch 1 cl 5(1); fork F5).
GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`, `the last day so far` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day after s 37(2)` f `from` `the last day so far` MEANS
    IF     f's `the kind of action` EQUALS `defamation`
       AND (`the day the 2020 defamation amendments commenced` `is on or before` (f's `the day the cause of action accrued`))
       AND f's `a concerns notice was given`
       AND ((`the last day so far` `plus days` (0 MINUS 55)) `is on or before` (f's `the day the concerns notice was given`))
       AND (f's `the day the concerns notice was given` `is on or before` `the last day so far`)
    THEN (f's `the day the concerns notice was given`) `plus days` 56
    ELSE `the last day so far`

-- s 45(1): where the person entitled "is under a legal disability, the time ... shall ... be extended by the period or
-- periods for which the disability exists or continues after the time at which the right to bring the action or
-- proceeding arose"; s 45(2): "while he remains a child or while he is subject to a mental deficiency, disease or
-- disorder by reason of which he is incapable of reasoning or acting rationally in relation to the action"; s 45(3):
-- "No period of limitation shall be extended by this section to more than thirty years from the time at which the
-- right ... arose." Childhood ends on the 18th birthday (s 3(1)). One period of incapacity is taken (fork F7); days of
-- disability are counted once where childhood and incapacity overlap.
-- The time at which the right arose, for s 45: the accrual day (or the s 39 return day); for money charged on land or a
-- legacy, s 33(3): "For the purposes of section 45 of this Act the right to bring an action to recover money secured as
-- aforesaid shall be deemed to have first accrued at the time of such payment or acknowledgment, or at the time of the
-- last of such payments or acknowledgments".
GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the right arose for s 45` f MEANS
    IF     f's `the kind of action` EQUALS `money secured by a mortgage, judgment or lien or otherwise charged on land, or a legacy`
       AND f's `there was a later acknowledgment or payment`
    THEN `the later of` (`the accrual day s 39 gives` f) `and` (f's `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment`)
    ELSE `the accrual day s 39 gives` f

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the 18th birthday of` f MEANS (f's `the person's date of birth`) `plus months` 216

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of childhood after the right arose for` f MEANS
    IF ((`the day the right arose for s 45` f) `is before` (`the 18th birthday of` f))
    THEN `the days from` (`the day the right arose for s 45` f) `to` (`the 18th birthday of` f)
    ELSE 0

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the counted incapacity begins for` f MEANS `the later of` (`the day the right arose for s 45` f) `and` (f's `the day the incapacity began`)

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of incapacity after the right arose for` f MEANS
    IF     f's `the person was mentally incapable after it accrued`
       AND ((`the day the counted incapacity begins for` f) `is before` (f's `the day the incapacity ended`))
    THEN `the days from` (`the day the counted incapacity begins for` f) `to` (f's `the day the incapacity ended`)
    ELSE 0

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days counted twice for` f MEANS
    IF     (`the days of childhood after the right arose for` f) GREATER THAN 0
       AND (`the days of incapacity after the right arose for` f) GREATER THAN 0
       AND ((`the day the counted incapacity begins for` f) `is before` (`the earlier of` (`the 18th birthday of` f) `and` (f's `the day the incapacity ended`)))
    THEN `the days from` (`the day the counted incapacity begins for` f) `to` (`the earlier of` (`the 18th birthday of` f) `and` (f's `the day the incapacity ended`))
    ELSE 0

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of legal disability for` f MEANS
    (`the days of childhood after the right arose for` f PLUS `the days of incapacity after the right arose for` f) MINUS `the days counted twice for` f

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the 30-year limit for` f MEANS (`the day the right arose for s 45` f) `plus months` 360

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`, `the last day so far` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day after s 45` f `from` `the last day so far` MEANS
    IF (`the days of legal disability for` f) GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the earlier of` (`the last day so far` `plus days` (`the days of legal disability for` f)) `and` (`the 30-year limit for` f)
    ELSE `the last day so far`

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the incapacity still continues for` f IF
        f's `the person was mentally incapable after it accrued`
    AND (NOT (f's `the incapacity has ended`))

-- s 46A: "Where a cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate of a deceased person, the time limited for the
-- commencement of the action shall be extended by a period equal to the period between the death of the deceased and
-- the grant of probate or letters of administration ..., or by a period of twelve months, whichever is the lesser."
GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`, `the last day so far` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day after s 46A` f `from` `the last day so far` MEANS
    IF     f's `the action survives for a deceased person's estate`
       AND (f's `the day of the death` `is before` (f's `the day of the grant of probate or administration`))
    THEN `the earlier of` (`the last day so far` `plus days` (`the days from` (f's `the day of the death`) `to` (f's `the day of the grant of probate or administration`))) `and` (`the last day so far` `plus months` 12)
    ELSE `the last day so far`

-- The order: the period (ss 33-38, with s 36(1a) and s 39), then s 37(2), then s 45, then s 46A (fork F8). The invalid
-- tax period "cannot be extended" (s 38(3)), so none of ss 45, 46A touch it.
GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`the last day for` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF f's `the kind of action` EQUALS `damages for death or personal injury resulting from abuse suffered as a child`
        THEN `there is no last day: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 3A(1))`
        IF `the months in the period for` (f's `the kind of action`) EQUALS 0
        THEN `not covered by this encoding`
        IF `the period answer is not covered` (`the period for` (f's `the kind of action`) `accrued on` (f's `the day the cause of action accrued`) `with latency` (f's `the injury remained latent`))
        THEN `not covered by this encoding`
        IF (`s 39 applies to` f) AND (NOT (f's `the person liable has returned to the State`))
        THEN `the time has not started: it runs from the return to the State of the person liable (s 39)`
        IF f's `the kind of action` EQUALS `recovery of money paid as a tax that was invalid`
        THEN `the last day to commence the action is` (`the ordinary last day for` f)
        IF `the incapacity still continues for` f
        THEN `the time is extended while the incapacity continues, but not beyond 30 years after the right arose (s 45(1), (3)); at the latest` (`the 30-year limit for` f)
        OTHERWISE `the last day to commence the action is` (`the last day after s 46A` f `from` (`the last day after s 45` f `from` (`the last day after s 37(2)` f `from` (`the ordinary last day for` f))))

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Period answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period answer is not covered` `the answer` IF
        `the answer` EQUALS `not covered: a kind of action this encoding does not cover (Parts 2 and 3: land, rent, mortgages and trusts)`
     OR `the answer` EQUALS `not covered: a restitution claim that arose before 17 June 1993 (s 38(1)(b): the old period or 6 years after 17 June 1993, whichever expired first)`
     OR `the answer` EQUALS `not covered: a tax paid more than four months before 2 June 1994 (s 38(2)(b))`
     OR `the answer` EQUALS `not covered: a publication before 1 January 2006, to which the limitation law before the Defamation Act 2005 applies`

§§ `Duties with deadlines, as regulative rules`

DECLARE `Limitation party` IS ONE OF `the person entitled to bring the action`

DECLARE `Limitation act` IS ONE OF
    `commence the action`
    `give notice of the intended action`
    `bring the action so that the claim may be judicially determined`

-- ss 35, 36, 37, 38 and the rest: the action "shall be commenced within" the period "and not after". Clock: day 0 is the
-- day the cause of action accrued; the days allowed run to the last day worked out above.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Limitation party` `Limitation act`
`the action must be commenced within the time limited` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the person entitled to bring the action`
    MUST   `commence the action`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the person entitled to bring the action` BECAUSE "the action was not commenced within the time limited by the Limitation of Actions Act 1936"

-- s 45A(1): "notice of an intended action must be given within 6 years after the relevant date". Clock: day 0 is the
-- date of the incident. s 45A(7): a breach does not bar the action, but costs the damages and costs it names.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Limitation party` `Limitation act`
`s 45A(1) -- notice of the intended action must be given within 6 years after the incident` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the person entitled to bring the action`
    MUST   `give notice of the intended action`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the person entitled to bring the action` BECAUSE "s 45A(1): notice of the intended action was not given within 6 years after the incident (s 45A(7) then applies)"

-- s 45A(5): the defendant "may, by written notice ..., require the plaintiff, within 6 months after the date of the
-- notice, to bring an action so that the claim may be judicially determined". Clock: day 0 is the date of that notice.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Limitation party` `Limitation act`
`s 45A(5) -- the action must be brought within 6 months after the defendant's notice` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the person entitled to bring the action`
    MUST   `bring the action so that the claim may be judicially determined`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the person entitled to bring the action` BECAUSE "s 45A(5): the action was not brought within 6 months after the defendant's notice (s 45A(7) then applies)"

DECLARE `Time limit answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: it was done on or before the last day`
    `late: it was done after the last day`
    `still in time: it has not been done yet and the last day has not passed`
    `late: it has not been done and the last day has passed`
    `in time: there is no limitation period for an action for child abuse (s 3A)`
    `still in time: the time has not started to run, because the person liable has not returned to the State (s 39)`
    `not covered: the time limit for this kind of action is not worked out here`

-- On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED
-- means in time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it today would still be in
-- time. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Limitation party` `Limitation act`
      `the act` IS A `Limitation act`
      `the clock start` IS A DATE
      `it has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was done` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`the deadline` `the rule` `for` `the act` `from` `the clock start` `done` `it has been done` `on` `the day it was done` `as of` `today` MEANS
    IF `it has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person entitled to bring the action` `the act` (`the days from` `the clock start` `to` `the day it was done`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `in time: it was done on or before the last day`
         OTHERWISE `late: it was done after the last day`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person entitled to bring the action` `the act` (`the days from` `the clock start` `to` `today`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still in time: it has not been done yet and the last day has not passed`
         OTHERWISE `late: it has not been done and the last day has passed`

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`, `the last day` IS A DATE, `commenced` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day commenced` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`the commencement deadline for` f `ending` `the last day` `whether commenced` `commenced` `on` `the day commenced` `as of` `today` MEANS
    `the deadline` (`the action must be commenced within the time limited` (`the days from` (f's `the day the cause of action accrued`) `to` `the last day`)) `for` `commence the action` `from` (f's `the day the cause of action accrued`) `done` `commenced` `on` `the day commenced` `as of` `today`

GIVEN f IS A `Limitation facts`, `commenced` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day commenced` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`was the action commenced in time` f `commenced` `the day commenced` `today` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day for` f
    WHEN `the last day to commence the action is` d THEN `the commencement deadline for` f `ending` d `whether commenced` `commenced` `on` `the day commenced` `as of` `today`
    WHEN `the time is extended while the incapacity continues, but not beyond 30 years after the right arose (s 45(1), (3)); at the latest` d THEN `the commencement deadline for` f `ending` d `whether commenced` `commenced` `on` `the day commenced` `as of` `today`
    WHEN `there is no last day: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 3A(1))` THEN `in time: there is no limitation period for an action for child abuse (s 3A)`
    WHEN `the time has not started: it runs from the return to the State of the person liable (s 39)` THEN `still in time: the time has not started to run, because the person liable has not returned to the State (s 39)`
    OTHERWISE `not covered: the time limit for this kind of action is not worked out here`

§§ `s 45A -- a child's personal injury: notice, the defendant's notice, and what non-compliance costs`

-- s 45A(1): "If -- (a) a child (the plaintiff) suffers personal injury; and (b) the time for bringing an action for
-- damages is extended by this Act to more than 6 years from the date of the incident out of which the injury arose (the
-- relevant date), notice of an intended action must be given within 6 years after the relevant date by, or on behalf
-- of, the child to the person or persons alleged to be liable in damages (the defendant)." Exception: an intentional
-- tort sued on against the person who committed it needs no notice to that person; any other person alleged to be
-- liable gets notice. s 45A(2): "If the injury is alleged to have arisen out of a motor accident, the notice must be
-- given to the relevant third-party insurer." The time "extended by this Act" is worked out here from s 36 and s 45 for
-- childhood alone, with the cause of action accruing on the day of the incident (fork F9).
DECLARE `Notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: s 45A applies only where a child (under 18) suffers the personal injury (s 45A(1)(a))`
    `no: the time for your action is not extended by this Act to more than 6 years after the incident, so s 45A(1) requires no notice`
    `no: notice need not be given to the person who actually committed an intentional tort when the action is brought against that person (s 45A(1) Exception)`
    `yes: give notice of the intended action to the relevant third-party insurer (s 45A(1), (2)), within 6 years after the incident, by` HAS `the notice day` IS A DATE
    `yes: give notice of the intended action to each other person alleged to be liable, not the person who committed the intentional tort (s 45A(1) Exception), by` HAS `the notice day` IS A DATE
    `yes: give notice of the intended action to each person alleged to be liable in damages (s 45A(1)), by` HAS `the notice day` IS A DATE
    `the Act does not say whether s 45A applies to an action for child abuse, which has no limitation period (s 3A) rather than an extended one`

GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE, `the day of the incident` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Limitation facts`
`the facts of a child's personal injury born` `the date of birth` `injured on` `the day of the incident` MEANS
    `Limitation facts` WITH
        `the kind of action` IS `damages that include damages for personal injuries`
        `the day the cause of action accrued` IS `the day of the incident`
        `the injury remained latent` IS FALSE
        `the day the injury first came to the person's knowledge` IS `the day of the incident` -- placeholder: no rule reads it when not latent
        `there was a later acknowledgment or payment` IS FALSE
        `the day of the last acknowledgment or payment` IS `the day of the incident` -- placeholder
        `the person liable was absent from the State when it accrued` IS FALSE
        `the person liable has returned to the State` IS TRUE -- placeholder
        `the day the person liable returned` IS `the day of the incident` -- placeholder
        `the person's date of birth` IS `the date of birth`
        `the person was mentally incapable after it accrued` IS FALSE
        `the day the incapacity began` IS `the day of the incident` -- placeholder
        `the incapacity has ended` IS TRUE -- placeholder
        `the day the incapacity ended` IS `the day of the incident` -- placeholder
        `the action survives for a deceased person's estate` IS FALSE
        `the day of the death` IS `the day of the incident` -- placeholder
        `the day of the grant of probate or administration` IS `the day of the incident` -- placeholder
        `a concerns notice was given` IS FALSE
        `the day the concerns notice was given` IS `the day of the incident` -- placeholder

GIVEN `the day of the incident` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for notice under s 45A(1) after` `the day of the incident` MEANS `the day of the incident` `plus months` 72

GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE, `the day of the incident` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the time is extended to more than 6 years for a child born` `the date of birth` `injured on` `the day of the incident` IF
    CONSIDER `the last day for` (`the facts of a child's personal injury born` `the date of birth` `injured on` `the day of the incident`)
    WHEN `the last day to commence the action is` d THEN ((`the last day for notice under s 45A(1) after` `the day of the incident`) `is before` d)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day of the incident` IS A DATE
      `it resulted from child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it arose from an intentional tort` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is against the person who committed it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another person is alleged to be liable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it arose out of a motor accident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`the s 45A(1) notice answer` `the date of birth` `the day of the incident` `it resulted from child abuse` `it arose from an intentional tort` `the action is against the person who committed it` `another person is alleged to be liable` `it arose out of a motor accident` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the day of the incident` `is before` (`the date of birth` `plus months` 216))
        THEN `no: s 45A applies only where a child (under 18) suffers the personal injury (s 45A(1)(a))`
        IF `it resulted from child abuse`
        THEN `the Act does not say whether s 45A applies to an action for child abuse, which has no limitation period (s 3A) rather than an extended one`
        IF NOT (`the time is extended to more than 6 years for a child born` `the date of birth` `injured on` `the day of the incident`)
        THEN `no: the time for your action is not extended by this Act to more than 6 years after the incident, so s 45A(1) requires no notice`
        IF `it arose from an intentional tort` AND `the action is against the person who committed it` AND (NOT `another person is alleged to be liable`)
        THEN `no: notice need not be given to the person who actually committed an intentional tort when the action is brought against that person (s 45A(1) Exception)`
        IF `it arose out of a motor accident`
        THEN `yes: give notice of the intended action to the relevant third-party insurer (s 45A(1), (2)), within 6 years after the incident, by` (`the last day for notice under s 45A(1) after` `the day of the incident`)
        IF `it arose from an intentional tort` AND `the action is against the person who committed it`
        THEN `yes: give notice of the intended action to each other person alleged to be liable, not the person who committed the intentional tort (s 45A(1) Exception), by` (`the last day for notice under s 45A(1) after` `the day of the incident`)
        OTHERWISE `yes: give notice of the intended action to each person alleged to be liable in damages (s 45A(1)), by` (`the last day for notice under s 45A(1) after` `the day of the incident`)

GIVEN `the day of the incident` IS A DATE, `given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day given` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`was the s 45A notice given in time` `the day of the incident` `given` `the day given` `today` MEANS
    `the deadline` (`s 45A(1) -- notice of the intended action must be given within 6 years after the incident` (`the days from` `the day of the incident` `to` (`the last day for notice under s 45A(1) after` `the day of the incident`))) `for` `give notice of the intended action` `from` `the day of the incident` `done` `given` `on` `the day given` `as of` `today`

GIVEN `the day of the defendant's notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to sue after the defendant's notice of` `the day of the defendant's notice` MEANS `the day of the defendant's notice` `plus months` 6

GIVEN `the day of the defendant's notice` IS A DATE, `brought` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day brought` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit answer`
`was the action brought in time after the defendant's notice` `the day of the defendant's notice` `brought` `the day brought` `today` MEANS
    `the deadline` (`s 45A(5) -- the action must be brought within 6 months after the defendant's notice` (`the days from` `the day of the defendant's notice` `to` (`the last day to sue after the defendant's notice of` `the day of the defendant's notice`))) `for` `bring the action so that the claim may be judicially determined` `from` `the day of the defendant's notice` `done` `brought` `on` `the day brought` `as of` `today`

-- s 45A(7): "Non-compliance with a requirement of this section on the part of a plaintiff does not prevent the
-- plaintiff from bringing an action for damages but unless the court is satisfied that there is good reason to excuse
-- the non-compliance -- (a) no damages will be allowed ... for medical or gratuitous services provided before the date
-- the action was commenced; and (b) no legal or other costs incurred in contemplation of the action ... will be
-- allowed."
DECLARE `Non-compliance answer` IS ONE OF
    `nothing is lost: you complied with s 45A`
    `nothing is lost: the court is satisfied that there is good reason to excuse the non-compliance (s 45A(7))`
    `you may still sue, but no damages for medical or gratuitous services provided before the action was commenced, and no legal or other costs incurred in contemplation of the action, will be allowed (s 45A(7))`

GIVEN `complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court excuses it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Non-compliance answer`
`the s 45A(7) answer` `complied` `the court excuses it` MEANS
    IF `complied`
    THEN `nothing is lost: you complied with s 45A`
    ELSE IF `the court excuses it`
         THEN `nothing is lost: the court is satisfied that there is good reason to excuse the non-compliance (s 45A(7))`
         ELSE `you may still sue, but no damages for medical or gratuitous services provided before the action was commenced, and no legal or other costs incurred in contemplation of the action, will be allowed (s 45A(7))`

§§ `s 46 -- absence or imprisonment of the person entitled`

-- s 46: "No person shall be entitled to any further time beyond the period fixed by this Act within which to bring any
-- action or proceeding by reason of the fact that he has been absent from the State or imprisoned."
DECLARE `Reason for more time` IS ONE OF
    `I was absent from the State`
    `I was imprisoned`

DECLARE `Absence answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: being absent from the State gives you no further time (s 46)`
    `no: being imprisoned gives you no further time (s 46)`

GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Reason for more time`
GIVETH AN `Absence answer`
`the s 46 answer` `the reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `I was absent from the State` THEN `no: being absent from the State gives you no further time (s 46)`
    OTHERWISE `no: being imprisoned gives you no further time (s 46)`

§§ `s 47 -- a time limit of less than twelve months in another law`

DECLARE `Excepted action` IS ONE OF
    `none of these`
    `a criminal action`
    `an action to try the validity of an election or of title to an office`
    `an action to try the validity of an assessment, rate or loan made by or to a local government body`

DECLARE `Twelve months answer` IS ONE OF
    `you may bring it at any time within twelve months from when the cause of action arose, by` HAS `the twelve-month day` IS A DATE
    `s 47 does not help: the other law already allows at least twelve months from when the cause of action arose`
    `no: s 47 does not apply to a criminal action (s 47(2)(a))`
    `no: s 47 does not apply to an action to try the validity of an election or of title to an office (s 47(2)(b))`
    `no: s 47 does not apply to an action to try the validity of a local government assessment, rate or loan (s 47(2)(c))`
    `no: the court is of the opinion that the limitation is essential to the nature or purpose of the action (s 47(2)(d))`

-- s 47(1): "Where any Act, regulation, rule or by-law limits the time within which an action to which this section
-- applies may be brought to a period of less than twelve months from the time the cause of action arises, then,
-- notwithstanding that limitation, that action may be brought at any time within twelve months from the time the cause
-- of action arises." s 47(2): all actions except (a)-(d).
GIVEN `the day it arose` IS A DATE
      `the last day the other law allows` IS A DATE
      `the exception` IS AN `Excepted action`
      `the court thinks the limitation essential` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Twelve months answer`
`the s 47 answer` `the day it arose` `the last day the other law allows` `the exception` `the court thinks the limitation essential` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the exception`
    WHEN `a criminal action` THEN `no: s 47 does not apply to a criminal action (s 47(2)(a))`
    WHEN `an action to try the validity of an election or of title to an office` THEN `no: s 47 does not apply to an action to try the validity of an election or of title to an office (s 47(2)(b))`
    WHEN `an action to try the validity of an assessment, rate or loan made by or to a local government body` THEN `no: s 47 does not apply to an action to try the validity of a local government assessment, rate or loan (s 47(2)(c))`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the court thinks the limitation essential`
        THEN `no: the court is of the opinion that the limitation is essential to the nature or purpose of the action (s 47(2)(d))`
        ELSE IF `the last day the other law allows` `is before` (`the day it arose` `plus months` 12)
             THEN `you may bring it at any time within twelve months from when the cause of action arose, by` (`the day it arose` `plus months` 12)
             ELSE `s 47 does not help: the other law already allows at least twelve months from when the cause of action arose`

§§ `s 48 -- the court's general power to extend time`

DECLARE `Whose time limit` IS ONE OF
    `a limitation period in this Act, other than the one for an invalid tax`
    `the period for recovering an invalid tax (s 38(2))`
    `a time limit in another Act, regulation, rule or by-law`

DECLARE `Extension answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: s 48 does not apply to criminal proceedings (s 48(3)(a))`
    `no: the period for recovering an invalid tax cannot be extended (s 38(3))`
    `possibly: the court may extend a time limit set by another law to the extent, and on the terms, the justice of the case requires (s 48(1)); the claim must be endorsed with a statement that you seek an extension under s 48 (s 48(4))`
    `no: neither ground in s 48(3)(b) is met (a material fact learnt in the last 12 months of the period or after it, with the action instituted within 12 months of learning it; or a reasonable delay caused by the defendant's representations or conduct)`
    `no: a ground in s 48(3)(b) is met, but the court is not satisfied that in all the circumstances it is just to extend (s 48(3), (3b))`
    `yes: the court may extend the time (s 48(1), (3)); the claim must be endorsed with a statement that you seek an extension under s 48 (s 48(4))`

-- s 48(3)(b)(i): "facts material to the plaintiff's case were not ascertained by him until some point of time occurring
-- within twelve months before the expiration of the period of limitation or occurring after the expiration of that
-- period and ... the action was instituted within twelve months after the ascertainment of those facts". s 48(3a): a
-- fact is material only if "(a) it forms an essential element of the plaintiff's cause of action; or (b) it would have
-- major significance on an assessment of the plaintiff's loss" (an input: a judgment). "Within twelve months before the
-- expiration": ascertained after the day twelve months before the last day (fork F10).
GIVEN `the fact is material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was ascertained` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the day of instituting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the late discovery ground is met` `the fact is material` `the day it was ascertained` `the last day of the period` `the day of instituting` IF
        `the fact is material`
    AND ((`the last day of the period` `plus months` (0 MINUS 12)) `is before` `the day it was ascertained`)
    AND (`the day of instituting` `is on or before` (`the day it was ascertained` `plus months` 12))

-- s 48(1): the court "may extend the time so prescribed or limited to such an extent, and upon such terms (if any) as
-- the justice of the case may require"; s 48(3): this section does not "(a) apply to criminal proceedings; or (b)
-- empower a court to extend a limitation of time prescribed by this Act unless it is satisfied" of (i) or (ii) "and that
-- in all the circumstances of the case it is just to grant the extension of time". s 38(3): the invalid tax period
-- "cannot be extended".
GIVEN `the time limit` IS A `Whose time limit`
      `it is criminal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a material fact was learnt late` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was ascertained` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the day of instituting` IS A DATE
      `the delay came from the defendant's conduct and was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court finds it just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Extension answer`
`the s 48 answer` `the time limit` `it is criminal` `a material fact was learnt late` `the day it was ascertained` `the last day of the period` `the day of instituting` `the delay came from the defendant's conduct and was reasonable` `the court finds it just` MEANS
    IF `it is criminal`
    THEN `no: s 48 does not apply to criminal proceedings (s 48(3)(a))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the time limit`
         WHEN `the period for recovering an invalid tax (s 38(2))` THEN `no: the period for recovering an invalid tax cannot be extended (s 38(3))`
         WHEN `a time limit in another Act, regulation, rule or by-law` THEN `possibly: the court may extend a time limit set by another law to the extent, and on the terms, the justice of the case requires (s 48(1)); the claim must be endorsed with a statement that you seek an extension under s 48 (s 48(4))`
         OTHERWISE
             IF NOT (    `the late discovery ground is met` `a material fact was learnt late` `the day it was ascertained` `the last day of the period` `the day of instituting`
                      OR `the delay came from the defendant's conduct and was reasonable`)
             THEN `no: neither ground in s 48(3)(b) is met (a material fact learnt in the last 12 months of the period or after it, with the action instituted within 12 months of learning it; or a reasonable delay caused by the defendant's representations or conduct)`
             ELSE IF `the court finds it just`
                  THEN `yes: the court may extend the time (s 48(1), (3)); the claim must be endorsed with a statement that you seek an extension under s 48 (s 48(4))`
                  ELSE `no: a ground in s 48(3)(b) is met, but the court is not satisfied that in all the circumstances it is just to extend (s 48(3), (3b))`

§§ `s 50 -- dispensing with notice before action`

DECLARE `Dispensation answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 50 does not arise: no law requires you to give notice before the action`
    `yes: the court may dispense with the requirement to give notice before the action, at any time before or after the close of pleadings (s 50)`
    `no: the court dispenses with a notice requirement only if the justice of the case requires it (s 50)`

-- s 50: "Where any provision of an Act, regulation, rule or by-law requires a person to give notice of his intention to
-- bring an action, or of any claim that he intends to prosecute in an action, before the action is instituted in a
-- court, the court may, if the justice of the case so requires, at any time before or after the close of pleadings,
-- dispense with that requirement."
GIVEN `a law requires notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `justice requires it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Dispensation answer`
`the s 50 answer` `a law requires notice` `justice requires it` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a law requires notice`)
    THEN `s 50 does not arise: no law requires you to give notice before the action`
    ELSE IF `justice requires it`
         THEN `yes: the court may dispense with the requirement to give notice before the action, at any time before or after the close of pleadings (s 50)`
         ELSE `no: the court dispenses with a notice requirement only if the justice of the case requires it (s 50)`

§§ `ss 37A, 37B -- defamation: the single publication rule and the court's extension`

-- s 37A(6): "associate of a first publisher means -- (a) an employee of the publisher; or (b) a person publishing
-- matter as a contractor of the publisher; or (c) an associated entity (within the meaning of section 50AAA of the
-- Corporations Act 2001 ...) of the publisher (or an employee or contractor of the associated entity)".
DECLARE `Later publisher` IS ONE OF
    `the first publisher`
    `an employee of the first publisher`
    `a contractor of the first publisher, publishing as such`
    `an associated entity of the first publisher, or its employee or contractor`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Single publication answer` IS ONE OF
    `your time for the later publication runs from the first publication (s 37A(2)), on` HAS `the day time runs from` IS A DATE
    `your time for the later publication runs from that later publication itself, on` HAS `the day time runs from` IS A DATE
    `not covered: s 37A applies to later publications after 1 July 2021 (2020 Act Sch 1 cl 5(2), (3))`

-- s 37A(1): it applies if "(a) a person (the first publisher) publishes matter to the public that is alleged to be
-- defamatory ...; and (b) the first publisher or an associate ... subsequently publishes (whether or not to the public)
-- matter that is substantially the same." (2): the cause of action for the subsequent publication "is to be treated as
-- having accrued on the date of the first publication" for s 37 and s 37B(2). (3): not "if the manner of that
-- publication is materially different" (an input: the court's judgment, s 37A(4)).
GIVEN `the first publication day` IS A DATE
      `the first was to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later publication day` IS A DATE
      `the later publisher` IS A `Later publisher`
      `it is substantially the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner is materially different` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Single publication answer`
`the s 37A answer` `the first publication day` `the first was to the public` `the later publication day` `the later publisher` `it is substantially the same matter` `the manner is materially different` MEANS
    IF `the later publication day` `is before` `the day the 2020 defamation amendments commenced`
    THEN `not covered: s 37A applies to later publications after 1 July 2021 (2020 Act Sch 1 cl 5(2), (3))`
    ELSE IF     `the first was to the public`
            AND (NOT (`the later publisher` EQUALS `someone else`))
            AND `it is substantially the same matter`
            AND (NOT `the manner is materially different`)
         THEN `your time for the later publication runs from the first publication (s 37A(2)), on` `the first publication day`
         ELSE `your time for the later publication runs from that later publication itself, on` `the later publication day`

DECLARE `Defamation extension answer` IS ONE OF
    `the court may extend the period, if you satisfy it that it is just and reasonable to allow the action to proceed, up to 3 years from the publication (s 37B(2)), that is to` HAS `the furthest day` IS A DATE
    `no: the court may extend the period only if the plaintiff satisfies it that it is just and reasonable to allow the action to proceed (s 37B(2))`
    `not covered: s 37B applies to publications after 1 July 2021 (2020 Act Sch 1 cl 5(4))`

-- s 37B(2): "The court may extend the limitation period to a period of up to 3 years running from the date of the
-- alleged publication of the matter if the plaintiff satisfies the court that it is just and reasonable to allow an
-- action to proceed." 3 years running from the date: fork F1 (the same day three years later).
GIVEN `the publication day` IS A DATE, `the court is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Defamation extension answer`
`the s 37B answer` `the publication day` `the court is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the publication day` `is before` `the day the 2020 defamation amendments commenced`
    THEN `not covered: s 37B applies to publications after 1 July 2021 (2020 Act Sch 1 cl 5(4))`
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied`
         THEN `the court may extend the period, if you satisfy it that it is just and reasonable to allow the action to proceed, up to 3 years from the publication (s 37B(2)), that is to` (`the publication day` `plus months` 36)
         ELSE `no: the court may extend the period only if the plaintiff satisfies it that it is just and reasonable to allow the action to proceed (s 37B(2))`

§§ `s 38(2)-(3b) -- recovering an invalid tax: the windfall rule`

-- s 38(3a): the action "may be maintained only to the extent the person bringing the action satisfies the court that
-- recovery of the money would not result in a windfall profit"; s 38(3b): it "would result in a windfall profit to the
-- extent the person ... (a) has passed on the burden of making the payment to another person; and (b) has not paid
-- back, or entered into an enforceable agreement to pay back, the amount of the payment." The amount recoverable is
-- the amount paid less the part passed on and not paid back (fork F11: "the amount of the payment" read as the part
-- passed on).
GIVEN `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER, `the amount passed on` IS A NUMBER, `the amount paid back` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the invalid tax recoverable from` `the amount paid` `passed on` `the amount passed on` `paid back` `the amount paid back` MEANS
    IF `the windfall part` GREATER THAN `the amount paid`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the amount paid` MINUS `the windfall part`
    WHERE
        `the windfall part` MEANS IF `the amount passed on` GREATER THAN `the amount paid back` THEN `the amount passed on` MINUS `the amount paid back` ELSE 0
